    Source Documents/Documentation/REvised/AKAD_Requirements_Analysis_Documentation.md:141:### FR-02 — Type: Functional Priority: Must
    Source Documents/Documentation/REvised/AKAD_Requirements_Analysis_Documentation.md:147:Acceptance Criteria: The owner can create and update a customer (name, contact number, Messenger handle), find the customer through search, and view all bookings linked to that customer.
    Source Documents/Documentation/REvised/AKAD_Requirements_Analysis_Documentation.md:159:Acceptance Criteria: The owner can create a package containing a name, description, inclusions, price, duration, deposit requirement, promotion period, and status. An inactive package, or a promotional package outside its promotion period, cannot be selected for a new booking but remains visible in historical bookings.
    Source Documents/Documentation/REvised/AKAD_Requirements_Analysis_Documentation.md:171:Acceptance Criteria: A booking cannot be saved without its customer, service, date, start time, end time, and location. A saved booking receives a unique reference and retains its package name, package price, and agreed total. Booking status is one of Pending, Confirmed, Awaiting Completion, Completed, or Cancelled. A cancelled booking stays in history with its reason. Payment status (Unpaid, Partially Paid, Fully Paid) is derived from the outstanding balance.
    Source Documents/Documentation/REvised/AKAD_Requirements_Analysis_Documentation.md:177:### FR-05 — Type: Functional Priority: Must
    Source Documents/Documentation/REvised/AKAD_Requirements_Analysis_Documentation.md:183:Acceptance Criteria: All test bookings display the correct service, client, date, time, and status on one calendar. Approved overlaps are visibly marked.
    Source Documents/Documentation/REvised/AKAD_Requirements_Analysis_Documentation.md:195:Acceptance Criteria: Only Confirmed and Awaiting Completion bookings and active availability blocks block a service. A proposed same-service booking whose blocked interval overlaps any of them is identified as a conflict, including at the moment a Pending booking is confirmed. A booking for a different service remains permitted when that service has no conflict. An Awaiting Completion booking keeps blocking its service until the owner releases it.
    Source Documents/Documentation/REvised/AKAD_Requirements_Analysis_Documentation.md:211:Acceptance Criteria: The conflict screen shows the affected booking, client, schedule, and service. The owner can change the schedule, cancel a booking, or authorize the overlap. The system does not authorize an overlap without a reason. A successful override records the affected bookings, approving owner, reason, and timestamp, and the overlap remains visibly marked.
    Source Documents/Documentation/REvised/AKAD_Requirements_Analysis_Documentation.md:223:Acceptance Criteria: An active block appears in the availability result and prevents ordinary booking confirmation for the affected service and interval. A block without a service applies to all services. A deactivated block no longer prevents confirmation but remains in history.
    Source Documents/Documentation/REvised/AKAD_Requirements_Analysis_Documentation.md:231:Statement: The system shall record multiple payments for a booking, including amount, type, method, status, date, optional reference, and recording owner.
    Source Documents/Documentation/REvised/AKAD_Requirements_Analysis_Documentation.md:235:Acceptance Criteria: The owner can record multiple payments for one booking. Payment methods are GCash and MariBank. Completed booking payments reduce the outstanding balance. Payment references are optional. Refundable deposits are not counted as booking payments.
    Source Documents/Documentation/REvised/AKAD_Requirements_Analysis_Documentation.md:249:Acceptance Criteria: With test data of a PHP 1,000 deposit and deductions of PHP 100 and PHP 250, the system calculates a refundable amount of PHP 650. These figures are test data, not business rules. A deduction that would make total deductions exceed the amount held is rejected. Each deduction records the item or description, reason, amount, recording owner, and date.
    Source Documents/Documentation/REvised/AKAD_Requirements_Analysis_Documentation.md:263:Acceptance Criteria: Selecting a package with a checklist template creates booking-specific items with expected, released, and returned quantities and release and return conditions. Changing the template afterward does not change a checklist already stored for a booking.
    Source Documents/Documentation/REvised/AKAD_Requirements_Analysis_Documentation.md:275:Acceptance Criteria: The owner can record self-pickup, Lalamove, or owner-delivered as the method, the fee, who is responsible (customer, included in package, or owner), and notes.
    Source Documents/Documentation/REvised/AKAD_Requirements_Analysis_Documentation.md:287:Acceptance Criteria: When the blocked end time is reached, the booking moves to Awaiting Completion, the service remains unavailable, and an action-required notification appears and persists. The post-event review records equipment return, deductions, outstanding payments, and service readiness. The service becomes available only after the owner completes the review and manually releases it; the booking then becomes Completed.
    Source Documents/Documentation/REvised/AKAD_Requirements_Analysis_Documentation.md:299:Acceptance Criteria: Monthly Collected Revenue equals completed booking payments whose payment dates fall within the selected month. Pending payments, failed payments, unpaid balances, and refundable deposits are excluded. Deposits held and deductions are reported separately. The reports also list upcoming bookings, cancellations, approved overlaps, and the most frequently booked services and packages.
    Source Documents/Documentation/REvised/AKAD_Requirements_Analysis_Documentation.md:311:Acceptance Criteria: Booking cancellations, approved overlaps, package-price changes, payment changes, deposit deductions, refunds, post-event completion, service release, and owner-account changes record the owner, action, affected record, description, and timestamp. Audit entries cannot be edited or deleted through the system interface.
    Source Documents/Documentation/REvised/AKAD_Requirements_Analysis_Documentation.md:323:Acceptance Criteria: The owner can set default minutes per service. A new booking uses the service defaults, and the owner can override either value for that booking only. Allowances cannot be negative. Changing a default does not alter existing bookings.
    Source Documents/Documentation/REvised/AKAD_Requirements_Analysis_Documentation.md:329:### FR-17 — Type: Functional Priority: Should
    Source Documents/Documentation/REvised/AKAD_Requirements_Analysis_Documentation.md:335:Acceptance Criteria: A booking created or updated on one connected device appears on another connected device within 30 seconds without a full-page reload.
    Source Documents/Documentation/REvised/AKAD_Requirements_Analysis_Documentation.md:347:Acceptance Criteria: Customer, package, booking, payment, deposit, checklist, notification, and report workflows remain usable at representative desktop and smartphone widths without inaccessible controls or horizontal page overflow.
